/-!
# Complete example and regression build

This module imports the three public facades and the checked examples.
Main theorems, hypotheses and support qualifications live in
`Thesis.Probability`, `Thesis.Causality` and `Thesis.CausalTransport`.
Each example states its fixture, original query, and the limit of what a
negative check refutes.

`HedgeChannelCompleteness` inhabits `ObservedGraph.publishedCompleteness`
for the value-rich positive class. `HiddenDAGCorrespondence` and
`HiddenDAGSupportedCorrespondence` transfer that package to original finite
hidden DAGs, including supported-zero domains with explicit used conditionals.
Restricted hedge constructions keep their geometric hypotheses at their
owners; they are not the general completeness proof.

Checked negative examples include `IdentificationRegression` for the obsolete
ID recursion, `NativeKernelInterfaceObstruction` for metadata-only composition,
and `HedgeCarrierRouteObstruction` for the tested route-ready hedge family.
-/
